## 🔹 What is Abstraction?

Abstraction means **hiding unnecessary implementation details and showing only the essential features** to the user.

It focuses on **what an object does** rather than how it does it.

---

## 🔹 Abstract Classes

An **abstract class** is a class that is designed to be a base class for other classes.

It can contain abstract methods that the child classes are expected to implement.

An abstract class cannot normally be instantiated directly when it contains abstract methods.

---

## 🔹 Abstract Methods

An **abstract method** is a method that is declared in an abstract class but does not provide the complete implementation.

Child classes are required to provide the implementation of the abstract method.

---

